## Context

Unbounce lets marketers build campaign landing pages through a visual editor. I was the first offshore engineer on the team. I started by maintaining the existing editor.

## Editor v2

I then joined the two-person effort on the next version. The legacy editor moved from Module Federation to micro-frontends, and the new editor was built as server-side-rendered micro-frontends from the start, composed by a reconciliation layer. I built editor features such as text editing, using newer React patterns and observables.

## A hard stretch

The team went through a major reduction. I kept delivering through it, which meant ruthless prioritization of what a smaller team could support.

## What it taught me

Working across many parts of a large editor, alongside experienced engineers, broadened how I think about frontend architecture.
